E AX3072 1003-addr-nonliteral.ax:9:13-14 addr-nonliteral "`__addr` answers a literal's bytes: a non-literal argument has no interned bytes, and the address it yields is the value's header, not its text" #"not a literal" !"the emitter evaluates a non-literal like any expression, so what comes back is an address the caller never asked for" ?"spell the literal - `(__addr \"text\")` - or read bytes out of a value with `strData`"
